    {
      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research a replacement for `bubble_sort` in `src/est_matriz_seq.c`. Compare a general O(n log n) per-column sort against the baseline O(n^2) sort, preserving the ordering needed for median and mode and the existing metric/printing behavior. Benchmark on the fixed harness rather than assuming the asymptotic improvement wins for small columns; report correctness and measured time.\",\"B\":\"Optimize only mode computation in `src/est_matriz_seq.c`: after the column is sorted, count equal-value runs in one linear scan instead of the nested pairwise scan and per-column allocation in `moda_aux`. Preserve the intended rule: return -1 when all values are unique, and on a frequency tie keep the first value in sorted order. Avoid changing other metrics so the effect can be measured independently.\",\"C\":\"Investigate parallelizing independent column work for the ARM64, 4-core target. Keep each column's calculations and accumulation order intact, use no more than four threads, and avoid parallel overhead when the workload is too small (derive any threshold generically from dimensions/measurements, not test values). Measure a sequential fallback and parallel variants; retain this avenue only if the harness shows a net gain.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidates with correctness evidence against the unchanged oracle/harness and measured timings on this target. Benchmark A, B, and C individually, then measure promising combinations (especially A+B and combinations with C): do not assume gains are additive. Select the fastest valid measured result, preserving input/output behavior and general correctness for valid inputs; do not specialize to benchmark cases or alter tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, permissions, or target.\",\"analysis\":\"The supplied source is Problem B's descriptive-statistics program. The only automatic measurement is baseline experiment `baseline-e1`: correct on 4 cases, mean 0.009463456769784292 seconds (samples 0.009291545487940311, 0.009884141385555267, 0.009214683435857296), score 0.5. The target is ARM64 with 4 CPU cores and no GPU. The strongest source-grounded opportunities are the quadratic column sort and quadratic mode scan; independent columns also make bounded parallelism worth measuring, but the baseline is already short and no workload dimensions are provided, so speedups are hypotheses rather than assumptions.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"0c84a97cd829a95d60ebc75f077e3e7c72b2de6934b3640df5d013b5540536e6\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research a replacement for `bubble_sort` in `src/est_matriz_seq.c`. Compare a general O(n log n) per-column sort against the baseline O(n^2) sort, preserving the ordering needed for median and mode and the existing metric/printing behavior. Benchmark on the fixed harness rather than assuming the asymptotic improvement wins for small columns; report correctness and measured time.\",\"B\":\"Optimize only mode computation in `src/est_matriz_seq.c`: after the column is sorted, count equal-value runs in one linear scan instead of the nested pairwise scan and per-column allocation in `moda_aux`. Preserve the intended rule: return -1 when all values are unique, and on a frequency tie keep the first value in sorted order. Avoid changing other metrics so the effect can be measured independently.\",\"C\":\"Investigate parallelizing independent column work for the ARM64, 4-core target. Keep each column's calculations and accumulation order intact, use no more than four threads, and avoid parallel overhead when the workload is too small (derive any threshold generically from dimensions/measurements, not test values). Measure a sequential fallback and parallel variants; retain this avenue only if the harness shows a net gain.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidates with correctness evidence against the unchanged oracle/harness and measured timings on this target. Benchmark A, B, and C individually, then measure promising combinations (especially A+B and combinations with C): do not assume gains are additive. Select the fastest valid measured result, preserving input/output behavior and general correctness for valid inputs; do not specialize to benchmark cases or alter tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, permissions, or target.\",\"analysis\":\"The supplied source is Problem B's descriptive-statistics program. The only automatic measurement is baseline experiment `baseline-e1`: correct on 4 cases, mean 0.009463456769784292 seconds (samples 0.009291545487940311, 0.009884141385555267, 0.009214683435857296), score 0.5. The target is ARM64 with 4 CPU cores and no GPU. The strongest source-grounded opportunities are the quadratic column sort and quadratic mode scan; independent columns also make bounded parallelism worth measuring, but the baseline is already short and no workload dimensions are provided, so speedups are hypotheses rather than assumptions.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"84d5d5f768bc4f67a40e538b0d5da8b3\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"0c84a97cd829a95d60ebc75f077e3e7c72b2de6934b3640df5d013b5540536e6\",\"session_id\":\"bb7a58941e74486ba24267f2f526de8f\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"347696620be921a3586b0b3657e7da8c45342d263a90825e39c48428cfc76499\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":12766,\"output_tokens\":4456,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":3960}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":17222,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
